---
// Architecture component for MirDB product showcase
// Displays a visual diagram showing the LSM tree data flow architecture:
// Write Request -> WAL -> Memtable -> Immutable Memtables -> SSTables (Level 0 -> Level N)
---

<section data-testid="architecture-section" id="architecture" class="bg-white py-16 sm:py-24">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl text-center">
      <h2 data-testid="architecture-heading" class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-4xl">
        Architecture Overview
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-gray-600">
        MirDB uses a Log-Structured Merge-tree (LSM) architecture for optimal write performance and durability.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Architecture Diagram -->
    <div
      data-testid="architecture-diagram"
      class="mt-16 flex justify-center"
      role="img"
      aria-label="MirDB LSM tree architecture diagram showing data flow from Write Request through WAL, Memtable, Immutable Memtables, and SSTables"
    >
      <svg
        viewBox="0 0 800 500"
        class="w-full max-w-4xl h-auto"
        aria-label="LSM Tree Architecture Diagram"
      >
        <title>MirDB LSM Tree Architecture - Data Flow Diagram</title>

        <!-- Background -->
        <rect fill="#f9fafb" width="800" height="500" rx="8"/>

        <!-- Write Request Box -->
        <g transform="translate(340, 20)">
          <rect
            x="0" y="0" width="120" height="50"
            rx="8" fill="#3b82f6" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="2"
          />
          <text x="60" y="30" text-anchor="middle" fill="white" font-weight="600" font-size="14">
            Write Request
          </text>
        </g>

        <!-- Arrow: Write Request -> WAL -->
        <path d="M400 70 L400 100" stroke="#6b7280" stroke-width="2" fill="none" marker-end="url(#arrowhead)"/>

        <!-- WAL Box -->
        <g transform="translate(320, 110)">
          <rect
            x="0" y="0" width="160" height="60"
            rx="8" fill="#fbbf24" stroke="#f59e0b" stroke-width="2"
          />
          <text x="80" y="25" text-anchor="middle" fill="#78350f" font-weight="600" font-size="14">
            WAL
          </text>
          <text x="80" y="45" text-anchor="middle" fill="#92400e" font-size="11">
            (Write-Ahead Log)
          </text>
        </g>

        <!-- Arrow: WAL -> Memtable -->
        <path d="M400 170 L400 200" stroke="#6b7280" stroke-width="2" fill="none" marker-end="url(#arrowhead)"/>

        <!-- Memtable Box -->
        <g transform="translate(320, 210)">
          <rect
            x="0" y="0" width="160" height="60"
            rx="8" fill="#34d399" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="2"
          />
          <text x="80" y="25" text-anchor="middle" fill="#064e3b" font-weight="600" font-size="14">
            Memtable
          </text>
          <text x="80" y="45" text-anchor="middle" fill="#065f46" font-size="11">
            (Active Skip List)
          </text>
        </g>

        <!-- Label: "when full" -->
        <text x="490" y="250" fill="#6b7280" font-size="11" font-style="italic">
          (when full)
        </text>

        <!-- Arrow: Memtable -> Immutable Memtables -->
        <path d="M400 270 L400 300" stroke="#6b7280" stroke-width="2" fill="none" marker-end="url(#arrowhead)"/>

        <!-- Immutable Memtables Box -->
        <g transform="translate(300, 310)">
          <rect
            x="0" y="0" width="200" height="60"
            rx="8" fill="#a78bfa" stroke="#8b5cf6" stroke-width="2"
          />
          <text x="100" y="25" text-anchor="middle" fill="#4c1d95" font-weight="600" font-size="14">
            Immutable Memtables
          </text>
          <text x="100" y="45" text-anchor="middle" fill="#5b21b6" font-size="11">
            (Queue awaiting flush)
          </text>
        </g>

        <!-- Label: "minor compaction" -->
        <text x="510" y="350" fill="#6b7280" font-size="11" font-style="italic">
          (minor compaction)
        </text>

        <!-- Arrow: Immutable Memtables -> Level 0 SSTables -->
        <path d="M400 370 L400 400" stroke="#6b7280" stroke-width="2" fill="none" marker-end="url(#arrowhead)"/>

        <!-- SSTables Container -->
        <g transform="translate(100, 410)">
          <!-- Level 0 SSTables -->
          <rect
            x="0" y="0" width="180" height="70"
            rx="8" fill="#f87171" stroke="#ef4444" stroke-width="2"
          />
          <text x="90" y="25" text-anchor="middle" fill="#7f1d1d" font-weight="600" font-size="14">
            Level 0 SSTable
          </text>
          <text x="90" y="45" text-anchor="middle" fill="#991b1b" font-size="11">
            (May overlap)
          </text>

          <!-- Arrow: Level 0 -> Level N -->
          <path d="M190 35 L230 35" stroke="#6b7280" stroke-width="2" fill="none" marker-end="url(#arrowhead)"/>

          <!-- Label: "major compaction" -->
          <text x="210" y="25" fill="#6b7280" font-size="10" font-style="italic">
            major
          </text>
          <text x="210" y="55" fill="#6b7280" font-size="10" font-style="italic">
            compaction
          </text>

          <!-- Level 1+ SSTables -->
          <rect
            x="240" y="0" width="180" height="70"
            rx="8" fill="#60a5fa" stroke="#3b82f6" stroke-width="2"
          />
          <text x="330" y="25" text-anchor="middle" fill="#1e3a8a" font-weight="600" font-size="14">
            Level 1+ SSTable
          </text>
          <text x="330" y="45" text-anchor="middle" fill="#1e40af" font-size="11">
            (Sorted, non-overlapping)
          </text>

          <!-- Additional Level indicator -->
          <rect
            x="440" y="0" width="140" height="70"
            rx="8" fill="#94a3b8" stroke="#64748b" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="4"
          />
          <text x="510" y="30" text-anchor="middle" fill="#334155" font-weight="500" font-size="13">
            Level N
          </text>
          <text x="510" y="50" text-anchor="middle" fill="#475569" font-size="11">
            (Higher levels)
          </text>
        </g>

        <!-- Arrow marker definition -->
        <defs>
          <marker
            id="arrowhead"
            markerWidth="10"
            markerHeight="7"
            refX="9"
            refY="3.5"
            orient="auto"
          >
            <polygon points="0 0, 10 3.5, 0 7" fill="#6b7280"/>
          </marker>
        </defs>
      </svg>
    </div>

    <!-- Accessible description for screen readers -->
    <p
      data-testid="architecture-diagram-description"
      class="sr-only"
    >
      The MirDB architecture diagram shows the data flow in an LSM tree:
      1. Write requests first go to the WAL (Write-Ahead Log) for durability.
      2. Data is then written to the active Memtable, an in-memory skip list.
      3. When the Memtable is full, it becomes immutable and joins a queue.
      4. Minor compaction flushes immutable memtables to Level 0 SSTables.
      5. Major compaction merges SSTables from Level 0 to higher levels, maintaining sorted order.
    </p>

    <!-- Architecture components description -->
    <div class="mt-12 mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <div class="grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="rounded-lg bg-gray-50 p-6">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">Write Path</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
            All writes go through the WAL first for durability, then to the active Memtable in memory.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg bg-gray-50 p-6">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">Compaction</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
            Background threads merge data from memory to disk, organizing SSTables across levels.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
